<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
<question type="stack">
<name>
<text>Create randomised stack entitled hypothesis</text>
</name>
<questiontext format="html">
<text><![CDATA[<p>A manufacturer claims that the mean lifetime of its batteries is \(\mu_0={@mu0@}\) hours. A researcher investigates whether the mean lifetime has
[[if test="is(tl=0)"]]decreased[[elif test="is(tl=1)"]]increased[[else]]changed[[/if]].
The population standard deviation is known: \(\sigma={@sigma@}\) hours. A random sample of \(n={@n@}\) batteries has a sample mean of \({@xbar@}\) hours. Assume the conditions for the test are satisfied and use a significance level of 5%. The null hypothesis is \(H_0:\mu={@mu0@}\).</p>
<p><b>(1)</b> Choose the alternative hypothesis \(H_1\).</p>
[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt_ans1]]
<p><b>(2)</b> Calculate the test statistic \(z\), to 2 decimal places.</p>
[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt_ans2]]
<p><b>(3)</b> Calculate the p-value, to 3 significant figures.</p>
[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt_ans3]]
<p><b>(4)</b> What is your decision at the 5% significance level?</p>
[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt_ans4]]
<p><b>(5)</b> Choose the correct conclusion in context.</p>
[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]] [[feedback:prt_ans5]]]]></text>
</questiontext>
<questionvariables>
<text><![CDATA[cs: rand(6);
tl: mod(cs,3);
rj: if cs<3 then 1 else 0;
mu0: 5*(rand(17)+8);
sigma: rand([4,5,6,8,10]);
n: rand([16,25,36,49,64]);
se: sigma/sqrt(n);
sg1: rand([-1,1]);
sg: if rj=1 then (if tl=0 then -1 else if tl=1 then 1 else sg1) else sg1;
zt: if rj=1 then (if tl=2 then 2.3 else 2.2)+rand(11)/10 else 0.3+rand(11)/10;
xbar: float(round((mu0+sg*zt*se)*100)/100);
z2: float(round(100*(xbar-mu0)/se)/100);
pf(zv,t):= if t=0 then float((1+erf(zv/sqrt(2)))/2) else if t=1 then float((1-erf(zv/sqrt(2)))/2) else float(1-erf(abs(zv)/sqrt(2)));
pv: pf(z2,tl);
pvs: significantfigures(pv,3);
wd: ["decreased","increased","changed"][tl+1];
tv5: if rj=1 then 1 else 2;
ta1: random_permutation([[0,is(tl=0),"\\(H_1:\\mu<\\mu_0\\)"],[1,is(tl=1),"\\(H_1:\\mu>\\mu_0\\)"],[2,is(tl=2),"\\(H_1:\\mu\\neq\\mu_0\\)"]]);
ta2: z2;
ta3: pv;
ta4: random_permutation([[1,is(rj=1),"Reject H0"],[0,is(rj=0),"Do not reject H0"]]);
ta5: random_permutation([[1,is(tv5=1),sconcat("There is sufficient evidence at the 5% level that the mean lifetime has ",wd)],[2,is(tv5=2),sconcat("There is insufficient evidence at the 5% level that the mean lifetime has ",wd)],[3,is(tv5=3),sconcat("The data prove H0 is true: the mean lifetime is definitely ",string(mu0)," hours")]]);
zw: z2+1;
pw: pf(zw,tl);
dw: if pw<0.05 then 1 else 0;
cw: if dw=1 then 1 else 2;
ph: pv/2;
pq: 1-pv;
tw1: mod(tl+1,3);
td4: 1-rj;]]></text>
</questionvariables>
<generalfeedback format="html">
<text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(tl=0)"]]
<p>\(H_0:\mu={@mu0@}\), \(H_1:\mu<{@mu0@}\) (left-tailed, since the researcher asks whether the mean has decreased).</p>
<p>\(z=\dfrac{\bar x-\mu_0}{\sigma/\sqrt n}=\dfrac{{@xbar@}-{@mu0@}}{{@sigma@}/\sqrt{ {@n@} }}={@z2@}\).</p>
<p>p-value \(=P(Z\le {@z2@})={@pvs@}\).</p>
[[if test="is(rj=1)"]]<p>Since \(p<0.05\), we reject \(H_0\): there is sufficient evidence at the 5% level that the mean lifetime has decreased.</p>
[[else]]<p>Since \(p>0.05\), we do not reject \(H_0\): there is insufficient evidence that the mean lifetime has decreased. This does not prove that the mean is {@mu0@} hours.</p>
[[/if]]
[[elif test="is(tl=1)"]]
<p>\(H_0:\mu={@mu0@}\), \(H_1:\mu>{@mu0@}\) (right-tailed, since the researcher asks whether the mean has increased).</p>
<p>\(z=\dfrac{\bar x-\mu_0}{\sigma/\sqrt n}=\dfrac{{@xbar@}-{@mu0@}}{{@sigma@}/\sqrt{ {@n@} }}={@z2@}\).</p>
<p>p-value \(=P(Z\ge {@z2@})={@pvs@}\).</p>
[[if test="is(rj=1)"]]<p>Since \(p<0.05\), we reject \(H_0\): there is sufficient evidence at the 5% level that the mean lifetime has increased.</p>
[[else]]<p>Since \(p>0.05\), we do not reject \(H_0\): there is insufficient evidence that the mean lifetime has increased. This does not prove that the mean is {@mu0@} hours.</p>
[[/if]]
[[else]]
<p>\(H_0:\mu={@mu0@}\), \(H_1:\mu\neq{@mu0@}\) (two-tailed, since the researcher asks whether the mean has changed).</p>
<p>\(z=\dfrac{\bar x-\mu_0}{\sigma/\sqrt n}=\dfrac{{@xbar@}-{@mu0@}}{{@sigma@}/\sqrt{ {@n@} }}={@z2@}\).</p>
<p>p-value \(=2P(Z\ge |{@z2@}|)={@pvs@}\) (the tail area is doubled).</p>
[[if test="is(rj=1)"]]<p>Since \(p<0.05\), we reject \(H_0\): there is sufficient evidence at the 5% level that the mean lifetime has changed.</p>
[[else]]<p>Since \(p>0.05\), we do not reject \(H_0\): there is insufficient evidence that the mean lifetime has changed. This does not prove that the mean is {@mu0@} hours.</p>
[[/if]]
[[/if]]]]></text>
</generalfeedback>
<specificfeedback format="html">
  <text></text>
</specificfeedback>
